    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0504" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12/1767: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hawks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-17T10:00:00-06:00">March 17, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 35, March 16, noon, as a result of
                    further conference with Foreign Office officials, changes on page 8 would read
                    as follows: lines 10 and 11<anchor n="56" xml:id="d438-f1"/> “evidence, with the
                    Brief and Reply Brief, as rebuts evidence, filed with the Answer and Brief, et
                    cetera”. Line 19<anchor n="57" xml:id="d438-f2"/> would read: “evidence filed
                    with the Answer or Brief, the additional evidence”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
